=== p2-windows · W7 · page:automations/AutomationBuilder (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:automations/AutomationBuilder   kind=page   web route=/automations/:id/edit
Web source  : web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationBuilderPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed + an empty/local feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "AutomationBuilderPage.xaml + AutomationBuilderPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto
  these real conventions (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Automations, matching the sibling builders
  TriggerConfigurator / ConditionBuilder / ActionBuilder / ConflictWarnings). The surface registers itself with the
  W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("AutomationBuilder", the RouteTable.cs L124-L125 entries for automations/new +
  automations/:id/edit) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the seven manifest data sources bind through the generated OpenAPI contract client behind
  an injected IAutomationBuilderFeed (P1/S8). AutomationBuilderClientFeed (AutomationBuilderPage.Source.cs) maps each
  hook to its generated operation id + path/body shaping, asserted via the FakeApiClient:
    useAutomation         -> get_api_v1_automations_id            (path id)            [GET /automations/{id}]
    useAutomationPreset   -> get_api_v1_automations_presets_presetId (path presetId)  [GET /automations/presets/{id}]
    useVehicles           -> get_api_v1_vehicles                                       [GET /vehicles]
    useNotificationChannels -> get_api_v1_notifications (NotificationChannel[])         [GET /notifications]
    useCreateAutomationFull -> post_api_v1_automations            (snake-case JSON body)[POST /automations]
    useUpdateAutomationFull -> put_api_v1_automations_id          (path id + JSON body) [PUT /automations/{id}]
    useTestRunAutomation  -> post_api_v1_automations_id_test_run  (path id)            [POST /automations/{id}/test-run]
  The write body is built by AutomationGraphCodec.SerializePayload — the native port of the web formToPayload +
  normalizeTriggerInput / normalizeConditionInput / normalizeActionInput — and round-trips with the load-time
  parsers (AutomationDetailSnapshot / AutomationPresetSnapshot.FromJson, the platform {data:…} envelope unwrapped).
  The default shell-registered page uses EmptyAutomationBuilderFeed (no-backend), exactly as the sibling W7 pages
  use their Empty*Feed; the generated-client feed is exercised by tests. No HTTP touches the view.
- The four web data states are reproduced as visible Fluent regions (ADR-006), driven by the edit-mode useAutomation
  query exactly as the web composes them: loading -> TsPageHeaderSkeleton + TsTableSkeleton shimmer
  (web isEdit && isLoadingAutomation); error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry (web isEdit && loadError);
  empty -> "Automation not found" TsEmptyState (web isEdit && !existingAutomation); success -> the builder form
  (web success / create / preset). Never a blank region.
- Panels: GlassPanel1/GlassPanel2 are the two branches of the When-section trigger panel (a tokenized TsGlassPanel)
  — the hosted native TriggerConfigurator when a trigger kind is chosen, else the empty-trigger TsEmptyState
  (web GlassPanel + EmptyState). GlassPanel3 is the create/preset preset-hint TsGlassPanel (web !isEdit GlassPanel).
  The When/Only-If/Then sections host the already-built sibling surfaces TriggerConfigurator / ConditionBuilder /
  ActionBuilder (seeded from the typed form graph; their geofence reads use local empty sources on the no-backend
  page). The web EditConflictBanner + DraftRecoveryBanner + unsaved-changes guard are reproduced via the native
  shared EditConflictBanner (resourceLabel = editConflict.resource.automation) + TsDraftRecoveryBanner
  (itemNoun = draft.noun.automation) + the cancel affordance's tooltip/AutomationProperties (forms.unsavedAutomation).
- Validation: AutomationValidator.Validate is the native port of the web validate() guard chain
  (name -> trigger -> trigger-place -> condition-place -> actions -> action-details), keyed off the six pre-resolved
  messages the projection surfaces; a failure drives the save-error banner (web saveError).
- i18n: all 41 manifest keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names. 34 builder keys + the 3
  cross-cutting keys (draft.noun.automation, editConflict.resource.automation, forms.unsavedAutomation) already
  existed in Strings/en/Resources.resw (shared with the sibling builder units); the 7 page-only keys
  (descriptionPlaceholder, emptyTrigger, onlyIfDesc, presetHint, subtitle, thenDesc, whenDesc) were added verbatim.
  The projection resolves every key unconditionally so catalog coverage is deterministic in every state/mode.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing physical fields on this builder surface — automation name/description, vehicle scope,
  enabled flag, and typed trigger/condition/action graphs only). Signal-threshold values are passed through verbatim
  exactly as the web does (no display-boundary conversion applies).
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel were linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the WinUI view is excluded —
  it uses Microsoft.UI; it is exercised by the app build). The sibling ActionBuilder/ConditionBuilder/
  TriggerConfigurator Model/Source/ViewModel were already linked, so the shared typed models are available headlessly.
- Build-time defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) BuildWhenSection declared a
  StackPanel return type but returned the TsFormSection (CS0029) — return type corrected; this CS error had cascaded
  into the WinUI XAML-compiler WMC9999 internal crash with spurious "Unknown type" noise on unrelated components
  (proven by isolating the C# error via the App-project CoreCompile), exactly the failure mode the sibling
  VehicleCostPage log documented; (2) the app project enforces CA1806 as an error, so the four ignored TriggerWire /
  AutomationActionKinds Try*-result calls in the parsers were made explicit discards (_ =); (3) the test file needed
  `using TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews;` for AutomationActionKind / AutomationChannel (the action types live in the
  parent namespace). All repaired; the solution builds 0 errors.

